From: electric-firebird
Subject: [PATCH] Under Emscripten, count committed metadata changes for the bridge

The browser bridge keeps each database's last statements prepared, and
empties that cache before DDL it runs itself. DDL it does not see (inside
EXECUTE STATEMENT, a procedure, another attachment) left kept statements on
the old metadata: Firebird 6 rebinds a prepared statement to the newest
metadata version but kept a dropped relation, so a kept SELECT of a dropped
table went on returning its rows.

A version DDL makes (create, alter, drop) is stored with CacheFlag::NOCOMMIT
and committed with its transaction by CacheElement::commit(); a first load
of an object commits at once, without the flag. This patch counts the former
in one process-wide atomic, fb_wasm_metadata_commits, which the bridge
compares on every statement it takes from its cache. Counting every
MetadataCache::mdc_front step instead would also count loads: 128 on an
attach, 9 on a procedure's first call, each emptying the cache for nothing.
Under __EMSCRIPTEN__ only; native builds are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/jrd/CacheVector.cpp b/src/jrd/CacheVector.cpp
index 274d3c4..3b6ea8f 100644
--- a/src/jrd/CacheVector.cpp
+++ b/src/jrd/CacheVector.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,10 @@
 using namespace Jrd;
 using namespace Firebird;
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+std::atomic<unsigned long long> fb_wasm_metadata_commits{0};
+#endif
+
 // class TransactionNumber
 
 TraNumber TransactionNumber::current(thread_db* tdbb)
diff --git a/src/jrd/CacheVector.h b/src/jrd/CacheVector.h
index 87b0ca7..1b85e08 100644
--- a/src/jrd/CacheVector.h
+++ b/src/jrd/CacheVector.h
@@ -41,6 +41,15 @@
 #include "../jrd/tra_proto.h"
 #include "../jrd/QualifiedName.h"
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+#include <atomic>
+// How many metadata changes (DDL: a created, altered or dropped object) have
+// committed in this process, in any database.  The browser bridge
+// (wasm/fb_wasm_api.cpp) empties its statement cache when this moves,
+// whatever ran the DDL.  Defined in CacheVector.cpp.
+extern std::atomic<unsigned long long> fb_wasm_metadata_commits;
+#endif
+
 namespace Jrd {
 
 class thread_db;
@@ -879,6 +888,12 @@ public:
 
 			if (flags & CacheFlag::NOCOMMIT)	// Committed newly created version in cache
 				pingLock(tdbb, flags, this->getId(), Versioned::objectFamily(this));
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+			// NOCOMMIT marks a version DDL made; a first load commits at once,
+			// without it, and is not a change.
+			if (flags & CacheFlag::NOCOMMIT)
+				++fb_wasm_metadata_commits;
+#endif
 
 			if (flags & CacheFlag::ERASED)
 				commitErase(tdbb);
